{"body":"## Summary\n\nRelated to stranske/Workflows#1836; unblocks the repo-owned test failure observed on generated sync PR #729 without editing that generated branch.\n\n<!-- workflow-source:sync_campaign -->\n\nThe unchanged-master test cleared only the in-memory dictionary. With _MASTER_FACTS_LOADED=false, the next lookup reloaded an unrelated on-disk entry, so its len(cache)==1 assertion became order-dependent. Isolate the cache path, dictionary, loaded and dirty flags using monkeypatch; restore globals after the test. Keep all reuse, no-redecode, and changed-file invalidation assertions unchanged. No production cache behavior, archive data or image processing is changed.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Reproduced the exact 2 != 1 failure by mocking a prior disk-cache entry before pytest.\n- The same seeded-cache reproduction passes after isolation.\n- `PYTHONPATH=src python3 -m pytest tests/test_judgement_surfaces.py -q --no-cov -o addopts=`: 37 passed, 1 skipped.\n- Four focused cache/persistence cases pass separately; Ruff and diff whitespace pass.\n\nAfter review/CI and merge, the owning sync campaign must refresh/revalidate #729 against the new base. Do not direct-merge the generated delivery.\n\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **Tests**\n  - Improved cache isolation in automated tests to prevent data from previous tests affecting lookup results.\n  - Ensured temporary test changes are restored after each test.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","closingIssuesReferences":[],"labels":[],"mergeCommit":{"oid":"c89de3fdb609a564d08c52fa8db4b3d72bb7ff3e"},"mergedAt":"2026-09-20T01:39:00Z","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-09-20T01:31:43Z","conclusion":"SKIPPED","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/stranske/Fine-Art-Archive/actions/runs/35481619988/job/106000354981","name":"cross-repo smoke","startedAt":"2026-09-20T01:31:44Z","s